{#
settings/_sidebar_peek.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
The peek switch in the Sidebar card (#699): whether a name too long for the
sidebar makes it lean out over the mail while the pointer is on it.

Posted on its own by settings--toggle to the endpoint the sidebar's drag handle
writes its width to (MailController::sidebarState), which answers with the
sidebar re-rendered, so the sidebar beside this switch starts or stops peeking
at once. The width itself has no control here: it is the edge of the sidebar,
which the sentence says.

Accepts nothing: reads the signed-in user.
#}
{% import '_partials/_segmented.html.twig' as seg %}

{% set name = 'settings.sidebar.peek.title'|trans %}
<div class="px-4 py-3 border-b border-line flex items-start justify-between gap-3"
     data-sidebar-peek-setting
     data-controller="settings--toggle"
     data-settings--toggle-url-value="{{ path('app_mail_sidebar_state') }}"
     data-settings--toggle-token-value="{{ csrf_token('sidebar_state') }}">
    <span class="flex items-start gap-3 min-w-0">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-arrows-left-right w-4 text-ink-faint mt-0.5 shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <span class="min-w-0">
            <span class="block text-xs font-medium text-ink-muted">{{ name }}</span>
            <span class="block text-[11px] text-ink-faint mt-0.5">{{ 'settings.sidebar.peek.hint'|trans }}</span>
        </span>
    </span>

    {{ seg.control('sidebar-peek', [
        { value: '1', label: 'settings.sidebar.peek.on'|trans },
        { value: '0', label: 'settings.sidebar.peek.off'|trans },
    ], app.user.sidebarPeek ? '1' : '0', {
        label:  name,
        width:  'w-28 shrink-0',
        action: 'change->settings--toggle#toggle',
        data:   { key: 'peek' },
    }) }}
</div>
